  "question": {
    "text": "A plano-convex lens fits exactly into a plano-concave lens. Their plane surfaces are parallel to each other. If lenses are made of different materials of refractive indices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is the radius of curvature of the curved surface of the lenses, then the focal length of combination is"
  },
